{"name":"Madonna","hex":"#3f4250","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Madonna","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Synonym of Mary, mother of Jesus, especially in Catholic contexts.","A female given name from Italian."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An artistic representation of the Virgin Mary, chiefly when holding the infant Jesus.","A morally pure woman."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Madonna"}],"entries":[{"title":"Madonna","blocks":[{"text":"Madonna Louise Ciccone is an American singer, songwriter, record producer, and actress. Dubbed the \"Queen of Pop\", she is known for her continual reinvention and versatility in music production, songwriting, and visual presentation. Her works, which concern social, political, sexual, and religious themes, have drawn acclaim and controversy. Regarded as one of the most influential musicians in history, Madonna broke gender barriers in popular music and has had a significant socio-cultural impact across her career."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/MadonnaO2171023_%2897_of_133%29_%2853269593787%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-MadonnaO2171023_%2897_of_133%29_%2853269593787%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Madonna","wikidata":"Q1744"},{"title":"Madonna (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Madonna is the debut studio album by American singer and songwriter Madonna. It was released on July 27, 1983, by Sire Records. In the late 1970s, Madonna had established herself as a singer in downtown New York City; alongside her Michigan boyfriend Stephen Bray, she put together a demo tape with four dance tracks and began pitching it around local nightclubs. She managed to get Mark Kamins, the resident DJ at Danceteria, to play \"Everybody\"—one of the songs from the tape. The song drew positive reception from the crowd, and Kamins took Madonna to Sire Records, where label president Seymour Stein signed her to a deal for three twelve-inch singles. Following its release on October 6, 1982, \"Everybody\" found success in the dance scene, and the label approved the recording of an album."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f6/Madonna%2C_debut_album_cover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Madonna_(album)","wikidata":"Q177943"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Madonna_-_Tampa_Bay_Times_%281985%29.jpg/500px-Madonna_-_Tampa_Bay_Times_%281985%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Madonna_-_Tampa_Bay_Times_%281985%29.jpg/1280px-Madonna_-_Tampa_Bay_Times_%281985%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Madonna_-_Tampa_Bay_Times_%281985%29.jpg/500px-Madonna_-_Tampa_Bay_Times_%281985%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Madonna performing in 1985 during the Virgin Tour","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMadonna_-_Tampa_Bay_Times_(1985).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Madonna_in_concert_wearing_fishnets_1987.jpg/500px-Madonna_in_concert_wearing_fishnets_1987.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Madonna_in_concert_wearing_fishnets_1987.jpg/500px-Madonna_in_concert_wearing_fishnets_1987.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Madonna performing during the 1987 Who's That Girl World Tour","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMadonna_in_concert_wearing_fishnets_1987.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Madonna